---
title: Hot cross buns
servings: 12
yield: 12 to 14 buns
tags: [british, easter, spring, vegetarian]
cuisine: british
time: 2 hours 45 minutes
source: Easy Hot Cross Buns by PJ Hamel, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/easy-hot-cross-buns-recipe
---

== Dough ==

Grease a #square baking pan{}(10 inch, or a 9 x 13-inch pan).

Warm the @apple juice{57%g}(or rum), @dried fruit{78%g} and @raisins{78%g}(or currants) together, covered, in the microwave until very warm. Let it cool to room temperature.

In a #large bowl{}, mix the @whole milk{283%g}(room temperature), @eggs{2}, @egg yolk{1}(keep the white), @unsalted butter{85%g}(room temperature), @instant yeast{2%tsp}, @light brown sugar{53%g}(packed), @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @ground cloves{1/4%tsp}(or allspice), @ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @table salt{11%g}, @baking powder{1%tbsp} and @all-purpose flour{540%g}.

Knead until soft and elastic. The dough is very slack, so grease your hands. Work in the cooled fruit and any liquid left with it.

Cover and leave ~{1%hour}, until puffy. It may not double.

Divide it into pieces about 3 3/4 oz (105 g) each, round them into balls and set them in the pan. Cover and leave ~{1%hour}, until puffed and touching. Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C) meanwhile.

Whisk the reserved egg white with @whole milk{14%g} and brush it over the buns.

Bake ~{20%minutes}, until golden brown. Turn them out of the pan in one piece and cool on a #wire rack{}.

== Icing ==

Stir the @powdered sugar{128%g}, @vanilla extract{1/2%tsp}, a pinch of @table salt{} and @whole milk{4%tsp} into a thick icing that will pipe, adding milk a drop at a time if needed.

When the buns are completely cool, pipe a cross on each one.

> To make them a day ahead and keep them soft, cook 3 tbsp of the flour with
> 1/2 cup of the milk, whisking, until thick, cool it and mix it in with the rest.
